  "term": "Zen Buddhism",
  "definition": "Zen Buddhism is described here as an Eastern philosophical tradition that uses nonverbal practices such as koans and silence to suspend ordinary language. In this account, it is presented as a way of going beyond the cognitive limits that linguistic habits can impose.",
